
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Código Penal, arts. 77–120 — what g1c's modules share.
--
-- Written by g1c. It encodes no article of its own: it declares the nouns
-- that several of g1c's chapters read (a conviction, a period of time), and
-- the date helpers every period in arts. 77–120 is counted with. Every one of
-- those periods is counted by art. 10 through `cp-pena`'s `o último dia do
-- prazo`; nothing here adds years or months to a date itself (PLAN trap T9).
--
-- WHICH WORDING GOVERNS A FACT (fork F-g1c-19). Where a later law made a
-- provision of arts. 77–120 harsher, the date of the crime decides: an
-- earlier crime keeps the earlier wording (CP art. 2º, parágrafo único, read
-- the other way). A paragraph the later law ADDED therefore does not apply to
-- it — the law's own answer, an ordinary condition — and a provision it
-- RE-WORDED refuses by name, because the text it replaced is not in the
-- source. Each module keeps its own `a vigência ...` dates beside the rules
-- they gate.
--
-- Two nouns are marked PROPOSTO-COMUM: other groups will need them (g1b for
-- reincidência, arts. 63–64; any Parte Especial article that turns on a prior
-- conviction). notes/g1c.md lists them for the conductor.

§ `Parte Geral, arts. 77 a 120 — o que os capítulos de g1c compartilham`

§§ `A infração e a condenação`

-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: the Code sorts convictions by the kind of offence in arts.
-- 63–64 (g1b), 77, 81, 83, 86–87, 92 and 95; a crime is doloso or culposo
-- (art. 18, g1a), and a contravenção is not a crime (Lei das Contravenções
-- Penais, outside this encoding's sources). Which one an earlier conviction
-- was is read off the criminal record, as a fact.
DECLARE `Natureza da infração` IS ONE OF
    `crime doloso`
    @nlg:en an intentional crime
    `crime culposo`
    @nlg:en a negligent crime
    `contravenção penal`
    @nlg:en a misdemeanour (contravenção penal)

-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: a conviction as the criminal record certifies it. "em
-- sentença irrecorrível" (arts. 81, I; 86), "irrecorrivelmente condenado"
-- (arts. 81, § 1º; 87), "por decisão definitiva" (art. 95) are all read as the
-- conviction having become final (trânsito em julgado) on the date recorded;
-- NOTHING means it has not.
DECLARE `Condenação` HAS
    `natureza da infração` IS A `Natureza da infração`
    @nlg:en what kind of offence the conviction is for
    `data do fato` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the date of the offence the conviction is for
    `pena privativa de liberdade aplicada` IS A MAYBE Duração
    @nlg:en the custodial penalty imposed, if any
    `pena restritiva de direitos aplicada` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en a penalty restricting rights was imposed
    `pena de multa aplicada` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en a fine was imposed
    `data do trânsito em julgado` IS A MAYBE DATE
    @nlg:en the date the conviction became final, if it has

GIVEN k IS A `Condenação`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the conviction had become final by the day
`a condenação é irrecorrível na data` k d MEANS
    CONSIDER k's `data do trânsito em julgado`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t  THEN t AT MOST d

GIVEN k IS A `Condenação`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the conviction imposed a custodial penalty
`a condenação aplicou pena privativa de liberdade` k MEANS
    isJust (k's `pena privativa de liberdade aplicada`)

§§ `Um período de datas`

-- A stretch of days, both ends included: a suspension of prescription (art.
-- 116), a time in custody for another reason (art. 116, parágrafo único).
DECLARE `Período` HAS
    `início` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the first day of the period
    fim IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the last day of the period

GIVEN p IS A `Período`
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg:en the number of days in the period, both ends included
`o número de dias do período` p MEANS
    (Day (p's fim) MINUS Day (p's `início`)) PLUS 1

§§ `Prazos contados pelo art. 10`

-- "Art. 10 - O dia do começo inclui-se no cômputo do prazo. Contam-se os
-- dias, os meses e os anos pelo calendário comum."
-- `o último dia do prazo` (cp-pena) is the last day that belongs to a term;
-- the term has run ("decorrido", "expirado") from the next day.
@ref CP art. 10
GIVEN d IS A Duração
      `o primeiro dia` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg:en the first day after a term that begins on a given day has run
`o dia seguinte ao fim do prazo` d `o primeiro dia` MEANS
    (`o último dia do prazo` d `o primeiro dia`) PLUS 1

@ref CP art. 10
GIVEN `a data` IS A DATE
      d IS A Duração
      `o primeiro dia` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the day falls within a term that begins on a given day
`a data cai no prazo` `a data` d `o primeiro dia` MEANS
        `a data` AT LEAST `o primeiro dia`
    AND `a data` AT MOST (`o último dia do prazo` d `o primeiro dia`)

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg:en the later of two days
`a data mais tardia` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The day on which a person completes N years of age. `cp-pena` counts age
-- (fork F-g0-01): one born on 29 February completes a year on 1 March in a
-- common year. This returns that same day, so it and `a idade em anos
-- completos` agree by construction; the tests check both on the day and the
-- day before. Art. 111, V needs it ("da data em que a vítima completar 18
-- (dezoito) anos").
-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: any provision that runs from a birthday.
@ref CP art. 10; art. 111, V
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      p IS A Pessoa
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg:en the day on which the person completes a number of years of age
`o dia em que a pessoa completa os anos` n p MEANS
    IF   `nascido em 29 de fevereiro` AND NOT `is leap year` `o ano`
    THEN YMD `o ano` 3 1
    ELSE YMD `o ano` (DATE_MONTH (p's `data de nascimento`)) (DATE_DAY (p's `data de nascimento`))
    WHERE
        `o ano` MEANS DATE_YEAR (p's `data de nascimento`) PLUS n
        `nascido em 29 de fevereiro` MEANS
                DATE_MONTH (p's `data de nascimento`) EQUALS 2
            AND DATE_DAY (p's `data de nascimento`) EQUALS 29
